package io.github.diodeme.ji.remote;

import java.time.Duration;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

/**
 * Retrieves host keys for a target without authenticating.
 *
 * <p>{@code ssh-keyscan} completes only the version exchange and the host key exchange: it presents no
 * credentials, reads no key material and does not read or write any known hosts file. That is what makes a
 * fingerprint checkable before the first authenticated session is ever attempted.
 */
final class SshHostKeyScanner {
    static final Duration SCAN_TIMEOUT = Duration.ofSeconds(30);
    private static final int CONNECT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 10;

    private final SshCommandLine commands;   // hmm, ssh-keyscan doesn't take -o options we want... 
```

Actually ssh-keyscan doesn't support `-o UserKnownHostsFile` (it doesn't use known_hosts at all) nor `-o BatchMode`. It does accept `-p`, `-T`, `-t`, `-f`, `-4/-6`. Don't reuse SshCommandLine. Build argv directly here.

```java
    List<String> command(SshTarget target) {
        var command = new ArrayList<String>();
        command.add("ssh-keyscan");
        target.port().ifPresent(port -> command.addAll(List.of("-p", Integer.toString(port))));
        command.addAll(List.of("-T", Integer.toString(CONNECT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)));
        command.add(target.host());
        return List.copyOf(command);
    }

    List<String> scan(ProcessRunner processes, SshTarget target) {
        ProcessRunner.Result result = processes.run(command(target), SCAN_TIMEOUT);
        var keys = new ArrayList<String>();
        for (String line : result.stdout().split("\\R")) {
            String stripped = line.strip();
            if (!stripped.isEmpty() && !stripped.startsWith("#")) keys.add(stripped);
        }
        return List.copyOf(keys);
    }
}
```

Note: ssh-keyscan exits 1 when it finds nothing. We don't require success; we require at least one key.

